.\" Generated by "sysml-grpc -man"; edit the description in the command's usage.go.
.TH SYSML-GRPC 1 "2026-08-30" "OpenSysML" "OpenSysML Manual"
.SH NAME
sysml\-grpc \- serve SysML v2 parsing, resolution and semantic services over gRPC
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sysml\-grpc
[options]
.SH DESCRIPTION
sysml\-grpc exposes the parser, name resolution and semantic services as a
network service, so a client in any language reaches the same engine the
command line and the language server use. It serves gRPC, gRPC\-Web and
Connect on one port by default, and caches the files it has parsed.
.PP
The standard library is the copy embedded in this binary unless
OPENSYSML_LIBRARY_PATH names another, and it is indexed in the background at
startup so the first model to arrive does not wait for it.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-cache\-size " int"
Maximum number of cached parsed files. The default is 100.
.TP
.BI \-cors\-allowed\-origins " string"
Comma\-separated exact origins allowed for browser CORS
.TP
.B \-exit\-with\-parent
Exit at end of file on stdin, so a child cannot outlive the process that holds
the write end of a pipe on it, SIGKILL included
.TP
.BI \-health\-port " int"
Health check HTTP port. The default is 8081.
.TP
.BI \-log\-level " string"
Log level (debug, info, warn, error). The default is info.
.TP
.B \-man
Write this command's manual page, in roff, to stdout and exit
.TP
.BI \-port " int"
gRPC server port. The default is 50051.
.TP
.B \-report\-address
Print the address to dial on stdout, as one line, once the listener is bound;
with \-port 0 this is how a client learns the port the kernel chose
.TP
.BI \-tls\-cert " string"
TLS certificate file for the main server
.TP
.BI \-tls\-key " string"
TLS private key file for the main server
.TP
.BI \-transport " string"
Transport to serve: connect (default; gRPC, gRPC\-Web and Connect on one
port), grpc (grpc\-go only), or stdio (an evaluation prototype over
stdin/stdout). The default is connect.
.TP
.B \-version
Show version and exit
.SH SERVING
.RS 2
.nf
# Serve gRPC, gRPC\-Web and Connect on port 50051
sysml\-grpc
# Let the kernel choose the port and report it
sysml\-grpc \-port 0 \-report\-address
# Serve grpc\-go only
sysml\-grpc \-transport grpc \-port 50051
# Speak the protocol over a pipe (a prototype)
sysml\-grpc \-transport stdio
# Serve over TLS
sysml\-grpc \-tls\-cert server.crt \-tls\-key server.key
.fi
.RE
.PP
Under \-transport connect the health endpoint is served as /health on the main
port, and \-health\-port 0 disables the separate listener, which is
deprecated.
.PP
A browser client needs its origin allowed: pass the exact origins to
\-cors\-allowed\-origins, separated by commas.
.SH ENDING THE SERVICE
The service shuts down gracefully on SIGINT or SIGTERM. With
\-exit\-with\-parent it also exits at end of file on stdin, so a service
started as a child cannot outlive the process holding the write end of that
pipe, however that process dies.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The status reports how the service ended:
.TP
.B 0
It shut down when asked, or reported what was asked of it.
.TP
.B 1
It could not serve: a port already bound, an unreadable certificate, a service
that failed.
.TP
.B 2
The command line could not be acted on.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B OPENSYSML_LIBRARY_PATH
Directory to load the SysML/KerML standard library from, instead of the copy
embedded in the binary.
.TP
.B OPENSYSML_MAX_STEPS
Expression evaluations one run may spend before it is reported as a runaway.
Default 10000000.
.TP
.B OPENSYSML_MAX_ACTION_STEPS
Token\-flow steps one action run may perform. Default 1000000.
.TP
.B OPENSYSML_MAX_EVENTS
Events one state machine run may dispatch. Default 1000000.
.TP
.B OPENSYSML_MAX_DO_STEPS
Do actions one state machine run may perform. Default 5000000.
.TP
.B OPENSYSML_MAX_ELEMENTS
Collection elements one evaluation may hold, which bounds the memory a run
holds rather than the work it does. Default 1000000.
.TP
.B OPENSYSML_MAX_CALC_DEPTH
Nested calc invocations one run may hold on the stack, which is what a
recursion spends. Default 10000, ceiling 25000.
.TP
.B OPENSYSML_MAX_SWEEP_RUNS
Runs one parameter sweep or sample may make, each a whole analysis or calc run
of its own with its own budgets. Default 1000.
.TP
.B OPENSYSML_JOBS
Runs of one check that may go concurrently \(em the linearizations of an
exploration, the engines \-engine all consults \(em each on a worker of its
own over the shared model; \-jobs and %jobs override it. Default the number of
CPUs.
.TP
.B OPENSYSML_TOOLS
Directory of the tool manifest: one JSON file per external tool (toolName,
version, executable, variables), each registered as the engine tool:<name>
that performs actions annotated ToolExecution with that toolName. Unset
registers no tool, and such an action is refused.
.TP
.B OPENSYSML_TOOL_TIMEOUT
How long one tool invocation may take, as a Go duration. Default 10s, after
which the performance fails.
.PP
Each variable above also answers to its legacy SYSML_\-prefixed name
(SYSML_MAX_STEPS for OPENSYSML_MAX_STEPS, and so on), which remains accepted.
When both are set and the OPENSYSML_ value is non\-empty, the OPENSYSML_ value
wins; setting only the legacy name prints a one\-time deprecation warning on
standard error.
.PP
A budget bounds one run \(em one evaluation, one instantiation, one calc
invocation, one action, one state machine \(em not a whole session, so a long
session of small operations never exhausts one. A run started inside another
shares the outer run's budget.
.SH REPORTING BUGS
Report bugs at https://github.com/Open\-MBEE/OpenSysML/issues.
.SH SEE ALSO
sysml(1), sysml\-lsp(1), https://github.com/Open\-MBEE/OpenSysML
